<html xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" xmlns:w="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<style>
  body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; line-height: 1.6; }
  h1 { color: #1A365D; }
  h2 { color: #2C4A7C; }
  .callout { background-color: #FEF3C7; border-left: 4px solid #ED8936; padding: 10px; margin: 10px 0; }
  .quiz { background-color: #F3F4F6; padding: 15px; border: 1px solid #E5E7EB; border-radius: 8px; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 15px 0; }
  th { background-color: #1A365D; color: white; padding: 10px; text-align: left; }
  td { border: 1px solid #CBD5E1; padding: 10px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<h1>Introduction to the Atom & Electron Configuration</h1>
<p>This is standard reading text. Write your normal paragraphs here. The importer will turn this into a Paragraph block.</p>

<h2>The Bohr Model</h2>
<p>Understanding the structure of the atom is fundamental to chemistry. The Bohr model helps us visualize where electrons live.</p>

<h3>Subatomic Particles</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Protons: Positively charged, found in the nucleus.</li>
  <li>Neutrons: Neutral charge, found in the nucleus.</li>
  <li>Electrons: Negatively charged, orbit the nucleus.</li>
</ul>

<div class="callout">
  <strong>Key Takeaway (Format: Start with >)</strong><br>
  > Remember: Protons are positive, Neutrons are neutral, Electrons are negative.
</div>

<h2>Electron Shell Capacities</h2>
<table>
  <tr>
    <th>Shell</th>
    <th>Formula</th>
    <th>Max Electrons</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>K</td>
    <td>2(1)² = 2</td>
    <td>2</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>L</td>
    <td>2(2)² = 8</td>
    <td>8</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>M</td>
    <td>2(3)² = 18</td>
    <td>18</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h2>Practice Quiz</h2>
<div class="quiz">
  <strong>QUIZ QUESTION</strong><br>
  What is the charge of a neutron?<br>
  - +1<br>
  - -1<br>
  - 0<br>
  <strong>Answer: 3</strong>
</div>

</body>
</html>
